RK628H fixes for the Rockchip BSP rk628 driver (kernel 6.1, develop-6.1)

Modified by Ground Plane Studio, LLC, 2026. GPL-2.0, as the driver it patches.

Fixes, all in the vendor driver:
- HPD is raised again after a userspace VIDIOC_S_EDID on F/H silicon
- the 1500 Mbps lane-rate clamp applies to RK628D only
- full I2S pin mux plus a master clock out, for boards with an I2S DAC
- the built-in EDID advertises basic audio
- D-PHY test registers are programmed while the PHY is held in reset
- CPLL at 1188 MHz so CEA pixel clocks divide exactly
- sync width, implausible mode and timing table fixes at 297 MHz
- dual MIPI only when the device tree declares the second port
- a watchdog that recovers the chip after an HDMI replug wedge
- continuous MIPI clock by default, needed above 60 Hz (a 'non-continuous-clk'
  device tree property turns it off)

